.TH DEECURE 1 "October 2026" "DeeCure 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deecure \- explains your Linux computer and helps fix it safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deecure
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.B status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deecure
.B history
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR WHEN ]
.RB [ \-\-kind
.IR KIND ]...
.RB [ \-\-fixes ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deecure
.B report
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR WHEN ]
.RB [ \-\-html
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deecure
.B fix
.RI [ ACTION " [" TARGET ]]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.br
.B deecure
.B undo
.I NUMBER
.br
.B deecure
.RB [ \-\-version | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deecure
asks the DeeCure agent what it found on this computer and shows it in plain
English. The agent runs in the background as a systemd user service, reads
the system every minute, keeps a short history, and runs rules that turn the
data into findings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Shows the open problems, most serious first. Each one has a severity
(Critical, Warning, or Info), a short title, an explanation, and the rule
that found it. If the agent has not checked the computer yet, it says so.
.TP
.B status \-\-json
Prints the same report as JSON, for scripts and servers.
.TP
.B history
Shows what changed on this computer, newest first, one heading per day:
packages (apt, dpkg, snap, Flatpak), configuration files, devices plugged in
and out, starts and unclean shutdowns, failed services, crashes, and the fixes
DeeCure made. The packages of one apt run are one line.
.B \-\-since
takes 30m, 24h, 7d (the default), 2w, or a date such as 2026\-10\-01.
.B \-\-kind
shows only packages, config, devices, system, services, crashes, or deecure,
and can be given more than once.
.B \-\-fixes
lists only DeeCure's fixes, with the numbers
.B undo
takes.
.TP
.B report
Summarizes a period (7 days by default): the health score and how it moved,
open problems, what changed, disks and when they fill up, and one tip.
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
saves it as one HTML file that works offline and prints well; a FILE of
.B \-
prints the HTML.
.TP
.B fix
Shows a fix's steps, with their commands and whether each can be undone, and
runs them after you say yes. Admin steps ask for your password.
.B \-\-list
lists every fix.
.TP
.BI undo " NUMBER"
Takes back a fix by its number.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Talk to the agent at
.I PATH
instead of
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/deecure/agent.sock .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Prints the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, output has no colors. Colors are also off when the
output is not a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was shown, whatever it contains.
.TP
.B 1
No answer, for example because the agent is not running.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/deecure/agent.sock
The agent's private socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deecure/deecure.db
The history and findings database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/deecure/rules/
The rules.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/krisskad0/DeeCure
